1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,096
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,096 --> 00:00:08,978
This morning the system named no pick, so tonight there is nothing to grade.

3
00:00:08,978 --> 00:00:13,700
No setup, no trade, no loss — that is the discipline working.

4
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:18,619
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

5
00:00:18,619 --> 00:00:24,009
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

6
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,739
On the day, the book is down 49 dollars.

7
00:00:28,739 --> 00:00:32,718
Arch Capital Group (ACGL) leads, +1.2 percent.

8
00:00:32,718 --> 00:00:35,053
argenx (ARGX) lags at -0.9.

9
00:00:35,053 --> 00:00:39,723
The checklist is clear: nothing requires action today.

10
00:00:39,723 --> 00:00:43,206
On screen, the day's gainers and laggards inside the paper book.

11
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:52,558
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

12
00:00:52,558 --> 00:01:00,076
6 positions, led by Arch Capital Group, ticker ACGL, AbbVie, ticker ABBV, argenx, ticker ARGX.

13
00:01:00,076 --> 00:01:10,953
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

14
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:17,658
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

15
00:01:17,658 --> 00:01:20,126
Every morning OROS proposes.

16
00:01:20,126 --> 00:01:30,972
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

17
00:01:30,972 --> 00:01:35,028
Inside the book today: 2 positions up, 3 down.

18
00:01:35,028 --> 00:01:37,496
Best, ACGL at +1.17 percent.

19
00:01:37,496 --> 00:01:39,348
Worst, ARGX at -0.95.

20
00:01:39,348 --> 00:01:44,462
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

21
00:01:44,462 --> 00:01:51,868
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -2.76% per trade over 1328 graded positions.

22
00:01:51,868 --> 00:01:59,099
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 50% position size.

23
00:01:59,099 --> 00:02:04,389
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

24
00:02:04,389 --> 00:02:17,086
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 170 names close the day in Stage 2; position size stays cut to 50% until the record earns it back.

25
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:20,963
Over to the sports desk.

26
00:02:20,963 --> 00:02:30,217
Day 97 of the race: three books, the same one hundred thousand simulated dollars, since July sixth.

27
00:02:30,217 --> 00:02:36,480
In first place, the live self-rebuilding book, in blue, at 107,899.

28
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:41,901
Then the index fund, in gray, 9.2 thousand back at 98,736.

29
00:02:41,901 --> 00:02:49,098
Then the frozen first portfolio, the green line, 9.3 thousand back at 98,594.

30
00:02:49,098 --> 00:02:51,715
The race has no finish line.

31
00:02:51,715 --> 00:02:56,015
Same books, same dollars, back at it tomorrow.

32
00:02:56,015 --> 00:03:00,876
Every line starts the same day with the same dollar.

33
00:03:00,876 --> 00:03:02,745
Nothing is restated.

34
00:03:02,745 --> 00:03:11,615
On screen, three equity lines grown from the same starting dollar: the frozen first book, the live book, and the index fund.

35
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:20,760
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

36
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:22,997
Nothing here is financial advice.

37
00:03:22,997 --> 00:03:25,979
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
